    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0568" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.626/115: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wallace</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-24T22:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1920—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 25—11:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>256. For War Trade Board and Davis. R–243.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1st.</label>
                    <item>Referring to our Rr–214.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d403-f1"/> In interview
                        today between Weinberg, Stephenson and Jacoby, Weinberg intimated individual
                        factories had somewhat changed their attitude since receipt of letter from
                        Mr. Polk and he feared that possibly Badi Pyrmont might be inclined to delay
                        Textiles Cartel orders in favor of any orders they might receive from
                        Kuttroff Pickhardt. Weinberg assured them he <pb facs="0569" n="479"
                            xml:id="pg479"/> would carry out contract loyally as far as his own
                        factory is concerned but could not altogether answer for others although he
                        would bring all possible pressure to bear.</item>
                    <label>2d.</label>
                    <item>Belgian Delegate on Reparation Commission intends urging Commission to
                        make ruling binding all Allies participating in dye stuffs options that they
                        will not order goods beyond amount needed for home consumption and will not
                        reexport them. Cable at once what attitude we should take. Rathbone.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
